---

<Layout
  title="The European Wildfire Index: Two Decades of Burned Land, Ranked by Country | Ranking Atlas"
  description={metaDescription}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLdArticle)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLdDataset)} />

<div class="bg-white">

  <!-- ═══ HERO ═══ -->
  <section class="pt-20 md:pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-ink/8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-brand font-semibold mb-3 text-center">Data Report</div>
      <h1 class="font-serif font-medium text-[1.75rem] md:text-[2rem] lg:text-[2.25rem] tracking-tight text-ink leading-[1.15] mb-3 text-center">
        The European Wildfire Index: two decades of burned land, ranked by country
      </h1>
      <div class="bg-bg-paper border border-ink/8 rounded-md p-6 mt-6 mb-8">
        <p class="text-body text-[15px] md:text-[16px] leading-[1.7] italic mb-4">
          Satellite mapping records 11.05 million hectares of Europe burned since 2006, an area larger than Portugal itself. Indexed against each country's size, the burden is starkly uneven: two countries have lost the equivalent of nearly a quarter of their entire land area, while France, the fastest-rising fire country in Western Europe, has already passed its worst full year on record with the peak of the 2026 season still ahead.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[13px] text-muted">By Daniel Grainger · Ranking Atlas · July 2026 · 12 min read</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Hero chart: France annual burned area -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-md border border-ink/8 p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="font-serif font-semibold text-[16px] text-ink leading-tight mb-1">France: annual EFFIS-mapped burned area, 2006–2026 YTD</div>
        <div class="text-[12px] text-muted mb-6">Hectares. 2026 is season to date (30 July). Previous record year (2022) and 2026 highlighted.</div>
        <div class="space-y-1.5">
          {franceYears.map((year, i) => {
            const ha = franceHa[i];
            const maxHa = 91024;
            const widthPct = Math.max((ha / maxHa) * 100, 0.5);
            const isRecord2026 = year === 2026;
            const isRecord2022 = year === 2022;
            const barColor = isRecord2026 ? 'bg-accent' : isRecord2022 ? 'bg-accent/60' : 'bg-brand-slate/40';
            const labelColor = (isRecord2026 || isRecord2022) ? 'text-accent font-semibold' : 'text-muted';
            return (
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <div class="w-[40px] text-right text-[11px] text-ink font-medium shrink-0">{year}</div>
                <div class="flex-1 h-5 bg-bg-paper rounded overflow-hidden">
                  <div class={`h-full rounded ${barColor}`} style={`width:${widthPct}%`}></div>
                </div>
                <div class={`w-[70px] text-right text-[11px] ${labelColor} shrink-0`}>{fmtNum(ha)}{isRecord2026 ? ' *' : ''}</div>
              </div>
            );
          })}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-3">* 2026 season to date (30 July). Source: EFFIS / Copernicus.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Embed block -->
      <details class="bg-bg-paper border border-ink/8 rounded-md mb-8">
        <summary class="px-5 py-3 text-[13px] font-semibold text-ink cursor-pointer select-none">Embed this chart</summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-4">
          <p class="text-[12px] text-muted mb-2">Copy and paste to embed with attribution:</p>
          <pre class="bg-white border border-ink/8 rounded p-3 text-[11px] text-body overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap"><code>&lt;iframe src="https://ranking-atlas.com/resources/european-wildfire-index" width="100%" height="620" style="border:none;" title="France burned area 2006-2026 | European Wildfire Index | Ranking Atlas"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:12px;margin-top:4px"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://ranking-atlas.com/resources/european-wildfire-index"&gt;The European Wildfire Index | Ranking Atlas&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- Anchor nav -->
      <nav class="bg-bg-paper border border-ink/8 rounded-md p-5" aria-label="Article sections">
        <p class="text-[14px] font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Navigation</p>
        <ul class="flex flex-col space-y-2 text-[14px]">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#key-takeaways" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">Key takeaways</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#season-2026" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">The 2026 season</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#decade-shift" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">The fires are moving north</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#burn-intensity" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">A quarter of two countries has burned</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#deadliest" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">Europe's deadliest fires</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#insurance-gap" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">The insurance protection gap</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#league-table" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">Two decades, country by country</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#methodology" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">Methodology</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full border border-ink/30 shrink-0"></span><a href="#download" class="text-brand hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline underline-offset-2">Download the data</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ OVERVIEW ═══ -->
  <section class="py-16 border-b border-ink/8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="space-y-6 text-body text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
        <p>
          The European Forest Fire Information System (EFFIS), the European Commission's satellite fire-mapping programme, has recorded every wildfire of approximately 30 hectares or larger across Europe since 2006. This study compiles that record into a single country-level index for 36 monitored countries: total area burned from 2006 to 2025, burn intensity normalised by national land area, decade-over-decade change, and a live layer covering the 2026 season to date.
        </p>
        <p>
          The figures were retrieved directly from EFFIS on 30 July 2026 and are stated as satellite-mapped totals throughout. To our knowledge, this is the first published index to rank every EFFIS-monitored country on normalised, like-for-like mapped data across the full two-decade record.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ KEY TAKEAWAYS ═══ -->
  <section id="key-takeaways" class="py-16 bg-bg-paper border-b border-ink/8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif font-semibold text-xl md:text-[1.5rem] tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight mb-6">Key takeaways</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-6 text-body text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
        <li><strong>11,051,539 hectares of Europe burned between 2006 and 2025</strong> across the 36 countries in the index, an area larger than Portugal, Hungary, or Austria.</li>
        <li><strong>France has already burned past its worst year on record.</strong> 91,024 hectares have been mapped in 2026 to date, against 66,337 hectares in all of 2022, the previous full-year record, with August, historically the peak month, still ahead. The season so far stands at 6.2 times France's twenty-year average.</li>
        <li><strong>Montenegro tops the burn-intensity index: 23.7% of its entire land area burned in twenty years.</strong> Portugal is second at 22.9% (2,109,543 hectares), Albania third at 17.9%.</li>
        <li><strong>France recorded a +656% increase in burned area decade-over-decade</strong> (2016–2025 vs 2006–2015), the largest rise of any major Western European country. The United Kingdom rose +513%, Türkiye +507%, Romania +3,288% from a low base.</li>
        <li><strong>Spain's 2026 season is running at 2.18 times its twenty-year average</strong> (206,768 hectares to date), twelve months after 2025 became its worst mapped year on record (393,079 hectares).</li>
        <li><strong>At least 400 wildfire deaths were recorded across the index countries 2006–2025, dominated by single catastrophic events.</strong> The Mati fire alone killed 104 people in one afternoon. Adjusted for population, Greece (20.8 deaths per million) and Portugal (12.1) carry an order of magnitude more of the human toll than any other country.</li>
        <li><strong>Greece's decade total was nearly flat (+2%)</strong> while Bosnia and Herzegovina (+134%), Croatia (+118%), Portugal (+121%) and Cyprus (+180%) all more than doubled.</li>
        <li><strong>The EU27's 2025 total of 1,079,538 hectares was the bloc's worst year on record,</strong> nearly double the 2006–2024 annual average, per the Joint Research Centre's annual wildfire assessment (JRC/EFFIS, March 2026).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ PULL QUOTE ═══ -->
  <section class="py-16 border-b border-ink/8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <PullQuote
        quote="We deliberately didn't model causes. The record speaks plainly enough on its own. France passing its worst full year on record in July, and the steepest twenty-year rises appearing in countries with no tradition of fire seasons, are facts of the mapping data. Why it's happening is a question for climate scientists; where it's happening is now documented."
        attribution="Daniel Grainger, founder, Ranking Atlas"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ THE 2026 SEASON (France record + season table) ═══ -->
